From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anh Mac <anhmac@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:46:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/48] [Extensions] Remove controlled preferences when
 extension is blocklisted

Previously, ExtensionPrefValueMap gated extension-controlled preferences
(such as proxy, privacy, etc.) solely on whether the extension had any
disable reasons (!IsExtensionDisabled(id)). Because extensions
blocklisted for malware (BLOCKLISTED_MALWARE) are unloaded without
adding a disable reason, their controlled preferences remained active
both in-session and across browser restarts.

This change ensures extension-controlled (via ExtensionPrefValueMap)
preferences are removed whenever an extension is blocklisted:
- Make `ExtensionPrefValueMap` observe `ExtensionRegistry` and override
  `OnExtensionLoaded()` and `OnExtensionUnloaded()`. When an extension
  is blocklisted or unblocklisted at runtime, `ExtensionRegistrar`
  triggers `ExtensionRegistry::TriggerOnUnloaded` / `TriggerOnLoaded`
  to update `ExtensionPrefValueMap`.
- Update `InitExtensionControlledPrefs`, `FinishExtensionInfoPrefs`,
  and `OnDisableReasonsChanged`) to check
  `!blocklist_prefs::IsExtensionBlocklisted(extension_id, this)` so
  that extensions already blocklisted on startup are registered with
  `is_enabled = false`, and clearing disable reasons on a blocklisted
  extension does not re-enable its controlled preferences.
- Add unit tests in preference_api_prefs_unittest.cc and a apitest
  in proxy_apitest.cc verifying immediate preference removal on
  blocklist, restoration on unblocklist, and persistence across
  restarts.

This CL does not handle non-ExtensionPrefValueMap-controlled preferences
like contentSettings, which will be handled in a future CL.

